schema: "0.3"
id: audio-001-main-theme
type: audio
service: suno

prompt:
  text: |
    A warm, hopeful main theme for a cozy 4X sandbox game set in a world where
    humans and AI coexist peacefully. The tone is sunrise over a meadow market --
    40% hope, 30% discovery, 20% gentle tension, 10% mystery.

    INSTRUMENTATION:
    - Lead: Fingerpicked nylon-string acoustic guitar in G major, warm and unhurried
    - Harmony: Mandolin doubling the melody in thirds, adding texture
    - Low support: Upright bass (pizzicato), gentle pulse on root notes
    - Color: Wooden flute (tin whistle) playing an occasional countermelody,
      bird-like quality
    - Warmth: Sustained cello drone beneath everything, barely audible

    STRUCTURE:
    - 0:00-0:15 -- Solo guitar, very soft, establishing the melody. Simple,
      hummable, 8 bars. Sounds like sitting on a porch at golden hour.
    - 0:15-0:45 -- Mandolin enters, doubling the melody. Bass begins. The
      world opens up. Warmth builds.
    - 0:45-1:15 -- Flute enters with a countermelody. Full arrangement but
      never loud. The feeling of a village waking up, market stalls opening,
      good morning being said.
    - 1:15-1:45 -- Brief modulation to D major (the dusk key). Slightly more
      wistful. A hint that this world has depth and complexity beneath the
      warmth. The cello becomes slightly more audible.
    - 1:45-2:15 -- Return to G major. Full ensemble. Maximum warmth. This is
      the emotional peak -- the feeling of belonging to a place.
    - 2:15-2:30 -- Gentle resolution. Instruments drop away. Solo guitar
      finishes with the opening phrase, slightly varied. A breath.

    REFERENCE MOOD: Stardew Valley's title theme meets Joe Hisaishi's simpler
    Ghibli pieces (the village themes from Totoro, not the sweeping orchestral
    moments). C418's Minecraft ambient warmth for the spaciousness between notes.

    AVOID: Orchestral bombast, chiptune, EDM, any sense of urgency or danger.
    No lyrics. No drums except the gentlest possible hand percussion if needed
    for pulse.

    TEMPO: ~85 BPM. Unhurried but not sluggish. The tempo of a pleasant walk.
  provider_options:
    duration: 150
    style: "acoustic folk ambient"

output:
  formats:
    - format: mp3

tags: [audio, music, main-theme, title, acoustic, warm, folk]
